{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler/stitch orchestrator) requests implementing srd024-expand requirements R2.1-R2.4, which add custom tab stop support (-t flag) to the `cmd/expand` utility. Specifically:\n   - R2.1: `-t N` sets uniform tab stop interval of N columns (tabs at N, 2N, 3N, ...)\n   - R2.2: `-t LIST` sets absolute column positions (comma/space-separated, strictly increasing). Tabs past the last position become a single space.\n   - R2.3: `-t` replaces the default interval of 8. Last `-t` wins if given multiple times.\n   - R2.4: When LIST contains a single value, it behaves identically to `-t N` (uniform interval).\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/expand/main.go` and `cmd/expand/expand_test.go`. Must add differential test cases and verify compilation and tests pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU expand tab stop behavior (default 8-column, custom uniform interval, custom absolute position list)\n   - Differential testing via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests against gexpand reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Manual argument parsing (existing code uses raw os.Args, not cobra)\n   - LC_ALL=C for consistent locale behavior\n   - Column tracking (1-indexed) with newline reset\n   - 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit per execution constitution\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd024-expand.yaml`\n     - Full SRD with R1 (default tabs, already implemented), R2 (custom tab stops, to implement), R3 (exit codes/SIGPIPE, already implemented), R4 (differential testing)\n     - Key detail: R2.2 specifies \"A tab at or past the last explicit tab stop is replaced by a single space\"\n     - Key detail: R2.2 supports \"comma-separated or space-separated positive integers in strictly increasing order\"\n\n   - `cmd/expand/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Currently only supports default 8-column tab expansion, no -t flag parsing\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd024-expand.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"bufio\"\n     \t\"fmt\"\n     \t\"io\"\n     \t\"os\"\n     \n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n     \tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     \tw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n     \texitCode := 0\n     \tif len(os.Args) <= 1 {\n     \t\texpand(os.Stdin, w)\n     \t} else {\n     \t\tfor _, name := range os.Args[1:] {\n     \t\t\tif name == \"-\" {\n     \t\t\t\texpand(os.Stdin, w)\n     \t\t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n     \t\t\tif err != nil {\n     \t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"expand: %v\\n\", err)\n     \t\t\t\texitCode = 1\n     \t\t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\texpand(f, w)\n     \t\t\tf.Close()\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     \tif err := w.Flush(); err != nil {\n     \t\tos.Exit(1)\n     \t}\n     \tos.Exit(exitCode)\n     }\n     \n     func expand(r io.Reader, w *bufio.Writer) {\n     \tbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\n     \tcol := 1\n     \tfor {\n     \t\tb, err := br.ReadByte()\n     \t\tif err != nil {\n     \t\t\treturn\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tswitch b {\n     \t\tcase '\\t':\n     \t\t\tspaces := 8 - (col-1)%8\n     \t\t\tfor range spaces {\n     \t\t\t\tw.WriteByte(' ')\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\tcol += spaces\n     \t\tcase '\\n':\n     \t\t\tw.WriteByte('\\n')\n     \t\t\tcol = 1\n     \t\tdefault:\n     \t\t\tw.WriteByte(b)\n     \t\t\tcol++\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/expand/expand_test.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Has 10 test cases all using default tab expansion (no -t args)\n     - Uses standard differential testing pattern with goBin/refBin/testutils.RunDiffTests\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main_test\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"os/exec\"\n     \t\"testing\"\n     \n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n     )\n     \n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n     \tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n     \trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gexpand\")\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary gexpand not found\")\n     \t}\n     \ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n     \t\t{Name: \"single_tab_at_col1\", Stdin: []byte(\"\\thello\\n\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"tab_after_one_char\", Stdin: []byte(\"a\\tb\\n\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"multiple_consecutive_tabs\", Stdin: []byte(\"\\t\\t\\n\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"tabs_at_various_positions\", Stdin: []byte(\"ab\\tcd\\tefgh\\ti\\n\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"no_tabs_passthrough\", Stdin: []byte(\"hello world\\n\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"empty_input\", Stdin: []byte(\"\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"newline_resets_column\", Stdin: []byte(\"abc\\td\\nabc\\td\\n\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"tab_at_tab_stop_boundary\", Stdin: []byte(\"1234567\\t8\\n\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"multiple_lines_mixed\", Stdin: []byte(\"a\\tb\\n\\tc\\nab\\tcd\\n\")},\n     \t\t{Name: \"tab_only\", Stdin: []byte(\"\\t\")},\n     \t}\n     \ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (contract only, not read)\n     - DiffTest struct: `{ Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; ... }`\n     - RunDiffTests signature: `func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)`\n     - Key: Args field is how we pass `-t` flags to both binaries\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The task was just starting (files were read, implementation had not begun).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that